ENGLISH
==============================================================================

THIS END-USER LICENCE AGREEMENT ("EULA") IS A LEGAL AGREEMENT BETWEEN YOU, THE END-USER, IN YOUR CAPACITY AS AN INDIVIDUAL AND/OR AS AN AGENT FOR YOUR COMPANY, INSTITUTION OR OTHER ENTITY (hereinafter referred to as the "Licensee"), AND HIS MAJESTY THE KING IN RIGHT OF CANADA, AS REPRESENTED BY THE MINISTER OF NATURAL RESOURCES (hereinafter referred to as "NRCan").

WHEREAS NRCAN HAS THE RIGHT TO GRANT A LICENCE FOR CANADA UTILITY RATES, A SOFTWARE TOOL AND WEBSITE THAT COLLECTS PUBLISHED ELECTRICITY AND NATURAL GAS RATES FROM OFFICIAL CANADIAN SOURCES AND PRESENTS THOSE RATES, MARKET PRICE HISTORY AND REPRESENTATIVE COST COMPARISONS (hereinafter referred to as the "Software").

BY DOWNLOADING, INSTALLING, ACCESSING, USING OR COPYING THE SOFTWARE, THE LICENSEE AGREES TO BE BOUND BY THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS BELOW:

1. DEFINITIONS
   1. "Software" includes the source code, scripts, configuration, tests, documentation and website files, and the databases, exports, representative models, analyses and compilations prepared by or for NRCan for Canada Utility Rates (including the Python package named canada-utility-costs), in every version, but does not include Third-Party Material.
   2. "Third-Party Material" means material that NRCan does not own, including: rate schedules, tariffs, rate orders, market data and other documents published by utilities, regulators, system operators (such as the IESO and the AESO), governments or other third parties, and the rate and price values they contain; the names and trademarks of those parties; and third-party software libraries and services used by the Software (such as Chart.js and the Python packages it installs).

2. GRANT OF LICENCE
   1. Upon the terms and conditions hereinafter set forth, NRCan hereby grants to the Licensee a non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the Software, including to view its source code where NRCan makes it publicly available and to install and run it for the Licensee's own use.
   2. Except with the prior written permission of NRCan, the Licensee shall not copy, reproduce, modify, adapt, translate, create derivative works from, publish, distribute, sell, sublicense, loan or transfer the Software or any part of it, or otherwise assign any rights under this EULA to any third party. Making a copy solely to install and run the Software under Article 2.1 is permitted.
   3. Viewing the source code of the Software and forking it on GitHub, to the extent permitted by the GitHub Terms of Service for public repositories, does not breach this EULA. Any other use, copying or distribution of a fork remains subject to this EULA.

3. TERM
   1. This EULA shall come into force upon the first instance that the Software is used by the Licensee or comes into the possession of the Licensee, and shall remain in force until it is terminated under Article 9 or until the Licensee stops using the Software and destroys all copies of it.

4. OBLIGATIONS OF THE LICENSEE
   1. The Licensee's publications referring to the Software, or quoting results displayed by it, must state the origin of the Software using the following text: "Canada Utility Rates is owned by His Majesty the King in Right of Canada, as represented by the Minister of Natural Resources © 2026".
   2. The Licensee may quote individual results displayed by the Software in the Licensee's own reports and publications, provided that Article 4.1 is met. This does not permit copying the source code, databases, exports or models of the Software, in whole or in substantial part.

5. MAINTENANCE AND SUPPORT
   1. The parties understand and agree that while the Licensee may report any bugs or technical malfunctions in the Software to NRCan, NRCan is under no obligation to provide technical support, maintenance services, update services, notices of latent defects, or correction of defects for the Software.

6. TITLE
   1. The Licensee agrees that the Software is and shall at all times remain the property of NRCan. The Licensee shall have no right, title and interest therein or thereto, except as expressly set forth in this EULA.
   2. The Licensee acknowledges that the Software is protected under the Copyright Act.

7. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
   1. NRCan claims no ownership of Third-Party Material, and this EULA grants no rights in it. Third-Party Material remains the property of its owners and is subject to their own terms and licences.

8. WARRANTY AND INDEMNITY
   1. The Software is licensed on an "AS IS" basis. NRCan makes no guarantees, representations, or warranties respecting the Software, either express or implied, arising by law or otherwise, including but not limited to effectiveness, completeness, accuracy, currency or fitness for a particular purpose. Rates, prices and representative models presented by the Software may be incomplete, estimated or out of date, and are not bills, quotes or offers of service. The Licensee should verify rates with the relevant utility or regulator.
   2. NRCan shall not be liable in respect of any claim, demand or action, irrespective of the nature of the cause of the claim, demand or action alleging any loss, injury or damages, direct or indirect, which may result from the Licensee's use or possession of the Software. NRCan shall not be liable in any way for loss of revenue or contracts, or any other consequential loss of any kind resulting from the Licensee's use or possession of the Software.
   3. The Licensee shall indemnify NRCan, its employees, contractors, agents and suppliers, from and against all claims, demands, losses, damages, costs, legal fees, actions, suits or proceedings that are in any manner based upon, arising out of, or attributable to the use, possession, or performance of the Software by the Licensee, or its employees or agents.

9. TERMINATION
   1. If the Licensee breaches any obligation under this EULA and fails to remedy the breach within thirty (30) calendar days, this EULA is deemed to be terminated immediately without any notice.
   2. Notwithstanding any other provision of this EULA, Articles 4, 6, 7, 8 and 10 shall survive termination of this EULA.

10. DESTRUCTION
    1. Prior to assigning, selling or otherwise disposing of any media, the Licensee shall completely erase or otherwise destroy any Software contained on such media.
    2. Upon termination of this EULA, the Licensee agrees to either:
       (1) Return to NRCan immediately all copies of the Software and any related documentation; or
       (2) Completely erase or otherwise destroy all copies of the Software as well as any related documentation on the Licensee's media.

11. APPLICABLE LAW
    1. This EULA shall be interpreted in accordance with the provincial or territorial laws in force in Ontario, Canada.

